<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n82624" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περκ-άζω</span></b> , (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέρκος</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περκνός</span>
			) <i>become dark, turn dark</i>, of grapes beginning to
			ripen, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀπώρα ἄκραισι περκάζουσα οἰνάνθαις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Chaerem.
					12.2
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅταν ἄρτι π. σταφυλή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thphr.
					<u>HP</u>
					9.11.7
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Hymn.Is.</u>
				168
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Am.</u>
				9.13
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅταν ἄρχωνται π. οἱ βότρυες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thphr.
					<u>CP</u>
					3.16.3
				</span></i>
			, etc. ; of olives, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Gp.</u>
				9.19.2
			</span></i> ; of flowers, <i><span class="en">
				Porph.
				<u>VP</u>
				44
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metaph., of
			young men, whose beard begins to <i>darken</i> their faces, <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Lav.Pall.</u>
				76
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Act.
			, <i>make dark-coloured</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				5.2
			</span></i>.</div>
